lazytv (1.1.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Read the HTTP response body by Content-Length instead of waiting for
    socket disconnect — commands no longer get lost on a slow TV.
  * Handle session expiry: on HTTP 401 the client emits sessionExpired,
    clears the saved session and returns to the pairing screen.
  * Parse ROAPError/ROAPErrorDetail so a rejected command reports why.
  * Block the pairing "request code" button for 60 s after a success
    (a repeated request invalidates the code shown on the TV).
  * Settings screen: show the version from the build instead of a
    hardcoded string.
  * Packaging: trailing newline in debian/{changelog,control,rules},
    add scripts/release-ppa.sh and release notes for 1.1.1.

 -- mindwork64 <vmurashov85@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:39:28 +0300
lazytv (1.1.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial release under the LazyTV name.
  * Renamed from lgremote to avoid trademark ambiguity.
  * No functional changes — same application, same features.

